<title>UK: Orange adds 86,000 customers in Q3.</title>
<headline>Orange adds 86,000 customers in Q3.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British mobile phone operator Orange Plc said it had added a net 86,000 subscribers in the third quarter, bringing its subscriber base to 659,000, giving it more than 10 percent of the total UK mobile phone market.  </p>
<p>Graham Howe, Orange's finance director, said the company's share of net market growth remained at around 30 percent. &quot;We look forward to continuing to build on our success,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Orange is poised to launch its autumn marketing campaign to drive increasing recognition of its services.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
